@startuml
title Workspace layout — three variants over one module library

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam maxMessageSize 250

package "contracts/ — one contract per Nargo package" {
  component "CMTATAztecLight\ncore token" as Light
  component "CMTATAztec\ncore + validation" as Base
  component "CMTATAztecDebt\ncore + validation + debt" as Debt
}

package "lib/ — cmtat_aztec_lib (type = lib)" {
  component "access_controlModule\nroles 1..11" as AC
  component "pauseModule\npause + permanent deactivation" as Pause
  component "enforcementModule\nper-address freeze" as Enf
  component "extraInformationModule\nterms + tokenId" as Extra
  component "validationModule\nblacklist / whitelist" as Val
  component "creditEventsModule" as Credit
  component "debtModule\nDebtIdentifier + DebtInstrument" as DebtM
}

Light --> AC
Light --> Pause
Light --> Enf
Light --> Extra

Base --> AC
Base --> Pause
Base --> Enf
Base --> Extra
Base --> Val

Debt --> AC
Debt --> Pause
Debt --> Enf
Debt --> Extra
Debt --> Val
Debt --> Credit
Debt --> DebtM

note as N1
  Noir has no inheritance and allows ONE contract per package,
  so a variant is a separate package composing a different subset
  of modules — not a subclass. Every user-callable entry point
  must be re-declared in that variant's own main.nr; a module
  method alone is not callable. The three main.nr files are
  therefore near-identical by construction.
end note

N1 .. Base

@enduml
